  "reputation": {
    "summary": "A niche cult part. On diyAudio one experienced listener puts it among the 'absolute best sounding' VFB op-amps (with LT1028, OPA132UA, LME49720HA) and calls it his favourite DIP op-amp: fuller bass and more detail than the LM4562, but sometimes thin on high violin notes. AudioKarma rollers preferred OPA2604. No measurement review exists.",
    "sonic_descriptors": [
      "fuller bass and body",
      "detailed",
      "sometimes too clear",
      "thin high violin notes"
    ],
    "typical_uses": [
      "DIP-8 op-amp rolling in CD players, DACs, preamps",
      "Upgrades in headphone amps and line stages",
      "SOIC-8 DIY audio stages, e.g. Rezzonics NuTube designs"
    ],
    "caveats": [
      "TI lists it Active but points to OPA1662 as a newer drop-in.",
      "The DIP version is reportedly scarce; most stock is SOIC-8, needing an adapter for socket rolling.",
      "Praise comes from a handful of listeners. A Head-Fi comment (unconfirmed) says it sounds unlike LM4562/LME49720/LME49860.",
      "AudioKarma advises careful decoupling against oscillation on sister LME49720; no LME49723-specific report.",
      "Split-supply part (±2.5 V minimum); one hobby project swapped it for an MCP6001 for low voltage."
    ],
    "sources": [
      "https://www.diyaudio.com/community/threads/the-best-sounding-audio-integrated-opamps.154106/page-37",
      "https://www.diyaudio.com/community/threads/the-best-sounding-audio-integrated-opamps.154106/",
      "https://www.head-fi.org/threads/lm4562-lme49720-lme49860-do-they-sound-different-to-you.521972/",
      "https://audiokarma.org/forums/threads/op-amp-upgrades-opa2604ap-obsolete.935775/",
      "https://audiokarma.org/forums/threads/opamp-question-lme49720-direct-sub-for-opa2134.434538/",
      "https://github.com/Rezzonics/NuTube_Overdrive_v1_1",
      "https://github.com/Rezzonics/NuTubeAmp"
    ]
  },
  "counterfeit_notes": "No LME49723-specific fakes reported, but sister LME parts are faked (remarked LME49710, tinytransistors.net 2022; fake LME49720NA on diyAudio). With the DIP scarce, distrust cheap marketplace 'LME49723NA' parts; buy LME49723MA/NOPB from TI, Mouser or DigiKey.",
